senses.gloss:
ब्राह्म॑ f. ई pertaining to (the) Brahman i.e. divine,
holy, spiritual;
 or pert. to Brahmans i.e. belonging or favourable to,
consisting of the sacerdotal class, Brahmanical. — f. ई E. of Durgā
or Sarasvatī;
 a woman married according to the Brahman rite.

ब्रह्मच॑र्य n. sacred study, the life and condition
of a Brahman student, esp. abstinence, chastity;
 poss. ˚वन्त्†.

ब्रह्मचारि॑न् a. poss. to ब्रह्मच॑र्य;
 m. a Brahman
student.

ब्रह्मण्य॑ a. devoted to sacred knowledge or friendly to
Brahmans;
 religious, pious i.g.

ब्रा॑ह्मण्य a. fit for Brahmans;
 n. state or dignity of a
Brahman, an assembly of Brahmans.

ब्रह्मदेय a. f. आ married after the Brahma rite, w.
विधि m. this rite itself;
 n. instruction in the sacred writings.

1 ब्र॑ह्मन् n. devotion (lit. swelling, sc. of the soul),
worship, piety, holy life, chastity;
 hymn of praise, prayer;
 sacred
text, magic formula, incantation, the syllable Om, the Veda, i.g. divine
science, theology or theosophy;
 the priestly or sacerdotal class;
 the
supreme Being regarded as impersonal, the Absolute.

2 ब्रह्म॑न् m. one who prays, any devout person or a priest;
a knower of sacred knowledge, a Brahman of caste or the priest so
called;
 the supreme Being, personif. as the highest god or creator of
the world.

ब्रह्मभूत a. entered into Brahman;
 n. the absorption
into Brahman.

ब्रह्मवर्चस॑ n. preeminence in sacred learning or
holiness, poss. ˚सि॑न् or ˚स्विन्;
 ˚स्य a. conducive to it.

ब्रह्मवि॑द् a. having sacred knowledge;
 m. theologian,
philosopher, sage.

ब्रह्मव्रत n. a cert. religious observance;
 the vow
of chastity, ˚धर a. performing it.

ब्रह्माञ्जलि m. joining the hands for the sake of (or
while studying) the Veda;
 ˚कृत a. performing it.

1 ब्राह्मण॑ m. a priest or theologian, a Brahman;
 f. ई a
woman of the priestly caste.

2 ब्रा॑ह्मण f. ई Brahmanical;
 n. the Brahman or
Absolute, sacred or divine power, a cert. class of Vedic writings.

ब्राह्मणाच्छंसि॑न् m. a cert. priest;
 ˚स्य॑ a.
belonging to him, n. his office.
